cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mera.jl in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Mera.jl: Fast, conservation-correct, code-agnostic analysis of astrophysical simulations in Julia"
abstract: >-
  Mera.jl is a Julia package for reading and analysing astrophysical simulation output. It reads
  RAMSES adaptive-mesh-refinement data (hydro, gravity, particles, clumps, radiative transfer)
  natively and in full. Formats are read through a reader registry, so the analysis layer works on
  the data rather than on the simulation code that wrote it, and a reader for another code can be
  registered from outside the package. It provides spatial selection, a derived-quantity registry
  with physical units, weighted profiles and phase diagrams, mass-conserving projections
  (axis-aligned and off-axis) and covering grids, a pluggable structure (clump/halo) finder, and a
  conservation-correct inflow/outflow flux-budget tool, all checked by a data-free correctness
  oracle. Readers for PLUTO, Chombo, Athena++, FLASH, GADGET and AREPO are in development on the
  multicode branch and are not part of a 1.x release.
type: software
